{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131419-alternative-familiar-ideas","id":1131419,"title":"Alternative Familiar ideas","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-19T13:32:33-07:00","id":1131419,"title":"Alternative Familiar ideas","content":"I love the idea of Familiars, but don't necessarily want something as alien as a spirit, as eerie as a ghost, or as obsessive as a goetia. I just came off a stint of playing Ars Magica (wonderful but very different game) where familiars are actually animals that you magically bond with for (among other things) companionship. Has anyone ever played at permanently enhancing an animal to use as familiar-ish companion?<br /> I was thinking of enhancing the creature with life and / or mind, as well as possibly bonding with him via mind, or possibly fate magic. I'm not really sure what effects to use, and I've never tried to put an indefinite effect on an animal before. Are there rules for this anywhere and / or does anyone have any ideas on how this may be workable in the game? I'm just looking for some direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T17:19:53-07:00","id":1131521,"title":"","content":"I would think that using Space magic could enhance your connection to an animal or person to the highest level, which could allow for some familiar-like effects. Life and Mind magic would only be useful to ''buff'' your living familiar. Any spells to replicate what familiars domismlike'y to be grounded in Space and Prime. Giving it a mana pool and draining/filling it would be Prime for sure. To make a familiar like that will require lasting spells or indefinite and relinquished spells for sure. But its actually doable.<br /> <br /> However, theres a good reason why anyone that wants an animal familiar just binds himself to the spirit of that animal and either let it manifest or possess an animal of its type, or even just plug ANY spirit into an animal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T18:13:19-07:00","id":1131538,"title":"","content":"Familiar is just a Spirit/Death/Mind 4 spell depending on the type of entity, so it stands to reason that you could create an animal familiar with just Life 4. The critical difference is that an animal does not have the human-level (though not human-<i>like</i>) intelligence of a spirit or goetia, so you can't really give commands or negotiate the terms of your relationship like you could with an ephemeral entity. Without further enhancements, it will behave like an animal. It doesn't have Essence of suffer bleed, either, so I think you'd want to make sure there's something else in it for the animal.<br /> <br /> And for the record, making any familiar requires Indefinite, possibly relinquished spells. The bond is created by the aforementioned Patterning spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T19:25:16-07:00","id":1131569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131419-alternative-familiar-ideas?p=1131538#post1131538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And for the record, making any familiar requires Indefinite, possibly relinquished spells.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Familiar spell doesn't need to be made Indefinite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T19:34:57-07:00","id":1131572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131419-alternative-familiar-ideas?p=1131569#post1131569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Familiar spell doesn't need to be made Indefinite.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does if you want the bond to last indefinitely. The Familiar spell grants the Familiar Merit for &quot;the Duration of the spell&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T20:09:54-07:00","id":1131582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131419-alternative-familiar-ideas?p=1131572#post1131572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It does if you want the bond to last indefinitely. The Familiar spell grants the Familiar Merit for &quot;the Duration of the spell&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did not realize RAW required indefinite / released status to maintain a standard spirit/ghost/goetia familiar - though I wasn't thinking of using an actual Familiar spell, since I didn't think there was such a thing for any non-ephemeral creature.<br /> I was thinking more along the lines of Cleverest of Things' suggestions. I wasn't thinking space since I rarely play mages with much skill in it, though I suppose it would work best for a link over a distance. I was thinking of buffing the animal with life and mind magic, but I realize that while I was thinking in terms of indefinite duration, I wasn't taking into account I would have to release the spells. Released spells can be their own special hassles.<br /> <br /> This may be harder than I thought.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T20:13:00-07:00","id":1131583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131419-alternative-familiar-ideas?p=1131521#post1131521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would think that using Space magic could enhance your connection to an animal or person to the highest level, which could allow for some familiar-like effects. Life and Mind magic would only be useful to ''buff'' your living familiar. Any spells to replicate what familiars domismlike'y to be grounded in Space and Prime. Giving it a mana pool and draining/filling it would be Prime for sure. To make a familiar like that will require lasting spells or indefinite and relinquished spells for sure. But its actually doable.<br /> <br /> However, theres a good reason why anyone that wants an animal familiar just binds himself to the spirit of that animal and either let it manifest or possess an animal of its type, or even just plug ANY spirit into an animal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't been satisfied with the last option because letting a spirit possess an animal seems like a really crappy thing to do to the animal. I was thinking of a familiar that was an animal, ally, and friend, not an animal I basically sacrificed to give a home to a spirit ally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T20:27:36-07:00","id":1131586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131419-alternative-familiar-ideas?p=1131583#post1131583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I haven't been satisfied with the last option because letting a spirit possess an animal seems like a really crappy thing to do to the animal. I was thinking of a familiar that was an animal, ally, and friend, not an animal I basically sacrificed to give a home to a spirit ally.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't have to be Possession, also in the same way that all objects have a dormant spirit in them so do animals. If an animal has its spirit awakened and fettered to it that animal isn't going to be abused by the spirit, just nudged toward being an exemplar of its species in order to generate Essence. It's probably the closest spirits get to being symbiotic rather than just parasitic, downside for the animal only really comes up if they have any other kind of spirit fettered to them, or if their native spirit gets warped. The spirit is also virtually immortal so eventually its host will die, that's kind of a bummer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T21:12:31-07:00","id":1131602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131419-alternative-familiar-ideas?p=1131572#post1131572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does if you want the bond to last indefinitely. The Familiar spell grants the Familiar Merit for &quot;the Duration of the spell&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, yes, true, but Familiar is also specifically one of the Merits you can requisition for a story with at least two dots of Status and a bit of wait time. Story length being what it is and requisitions being what they are, you can almost certainly manage a kind of fostering system for an Adept with an interest in familiar-lending or other uses of the wider setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T02:45:24-07:00","id":1131658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131419-alternative-familiar-ideas?p=1131582#post1131582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I did not realize RAW required indefinite / released status to maintain a standard spirit/ghost/goetia familiar - though I wasn't thinking of using an actual Familiar spell, since I didn't think there was such a thing for any non-ephemeral creature.<br /> I was thinking more along the lines of Cleverest of Things' suggestions. I wasn't thinking space since I rarely play mages with much skill in it, though I suppose it would work best for a link over a distance. I was thinking of buffing the animal with life and mind magic, but I realize that while I was thinking in terms of indefinite duration, I wasn't taking into account I would have to release the spells. Released spells can be their own special hassles.<br /> <br /> This may be harder than I thought.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, it's not spelled out directly at all. The Familiar Merit grants the Familiar Condition which states that it is created by the Familiar spell. And you were absolutely right, it's not a thing that exists. I only brought up the pre-existing Familiar spell because even if you decide that your animal companion isn't literally a Familiar in the mechanical sense, looking at how similar effects work and what they require is a good way to steer your Creative Thaumaturgy in the right direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T04:43:39-07:00","id":1131666,"title":"","content":"You could probably justify a single life/mind conjunctional spell that grants most of the benefits. Call it &quot;Living Familiar&quot; or something and note that it's not <i>technically</i> a familiar because it doesn't grant the manifestation but most mages consider it close enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T04:48:45-07:00","id":1131668,"title":"","content":"For a simpler version: Take a look at the bonded condition. I think it could even be established without magic, but a Life 2 or Mind 2 spell could probably also establish the condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T04:51:19-07:00","id":1131669,"title":"","content":"Also with Life 5 you can create a mindless shell of an animal for your familiar to possess. That neatly sidesteps the moral concerns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T05:57:05-07:00","id":1131674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131419-alternative-familiar-ideas?p=1131668#post1131668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For a simpler version: Take a look at the bonded condition. I think it could even be established without magic, but a Life 2 or Mind 2 spell could probably also establish the condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never noticed that condition. It isn't everything I wanted, but it is appropriate. I wonder how you achieve it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T06:00:57-07:00","id":1131676,"title":"","content":"By treating the animal well over the course of its life, or magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T06:02:02-07:00","id":1131677,"title":"","content":"It looks like the closest think I can get to what I want would involve the bonded condition, and several safely relinquished, indefinite spells, which is going to get expensive.<br /> <br /> Follow up questions on how to cast these spells, since I will want to give the Familiar abilities it can control. If I wanted to cast a Death effect on a dog to duplicate the effects of &quot;Touch of the Grave&quot;, but also wanted to give the dog the ability to turn that power on or off, how do you think I would I go about it? Would it require some kind of conjunctional Mind effect?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":532,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","user":"Newes","date":". 08-20-2017, 09:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T06:05:50-07:00","id":1131679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131419-alternative-familiar-ideas?p=1131586#post1131586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It doesn't have to be Possession, also in the same way that all objects have a dormant spirit in them so do animals. If an animal has its spirit awakened and fettered to it that animal isn't going to be abused by the spirit, just nudged toward being an exemplar of its species in order to generate Essence. It's probably the closest spirits get to being symbiotic rather than just parasitic, downside for the animal only really comes up if they have any other kind of spirit fettered to them, or if their native spirit gets warped. The spirit is also virtually immortal so eventually its host will die, that's kind of a bummer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly what I wanted, but interesting. I didn't realize individual animals had associated spirits that could be awakened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T06:20:25-07:00","id":1131681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131419-alternative-familiar-ideas?p=1131677#post1131677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Follow up questions on how to cast these spells, since I will want to give the Familiar abilities it can control. If I wanted to cast a Death effect on a dog to duplicate the effects of &quot;Touch of the Grave&quot;, but also wanted to give the dog the ability to turn that power on or off, how do you think I would I go about it? Would it require some kind of conjunctional Mind effect?</div> </div> </div> </div>Use the Fate Conditional Duration attainment set to, &quot;When the dog wants it to end.&quot; The dog will then end the spell whenever it wishes. The dog will have no power to turn it back on again, spells don't come with on/off switches, they're either going or they're not. The closest you can come to turning them on and off is to use spells or WP boosted Withstand to temporarily suppress them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 08-20-2017, 09:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T07:38:35-07:00","id":1131700,"title":"","content":"I think the Fate 2 spell Warding Gesture can be utilized to enable a spell turning on/off repeatedly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T08:07:33-07:00","id":1131715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131419-alternative-familiar-ideas?p=1131700#post1131700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Fate 2 spell Warding Gesture can be utilized to enable a spell turning on/off repeatedly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see how.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T08:09:14-07:00","id":1131719,"title":"","content":"You could also set up a spell with a conditional duration, then use a dispel on it with another conditional duration, and then dispel that dispel spell with <i>another </i>conditional duration. <br /> <br /> So you can turn it off by ending the second dispellation, turn it back on by ending the first, and then turn it off again by ending the spell itself. <br /> <br /> Theoretically you can keep adding layers, but it gets a bit control-intensive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T08:28:24-07:00","id":1131728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131419-alternative-familiar-ideas?p=1131679#post1131679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not exactly what I wanted, but interesting. I didn't realize individual animals had associated spirits that could be awakened.</div> </div> </div> </div>Every individual thing (other than humans) has a spirit. Or had one at some point, anyway. When a tree sprouts, an animal is born or a building goes up, a mote is born. This also goes for fleeting things like emotions; whenever a human gets sad, a baby sadness-spirit comes into existence, though it usually starves to death sooner rather than later as the human's mood changes and the sadness-Essence dries up. Animal-spirits are a little more resilient since they usually have at least the entire lifespan of their associated animal to build up strength, but the real heavy-hitters are the spirits of elements and geological features since their Essence founts are nearly inextinguishable.<br /> <br /> All of that is presuming a bigger spirit doesn't just come along and eat them, of course.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131419-alternative-familiar-ideas?p=1131681#post1131681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Use the Fate Conditional Duration attainment set to, &quot;When the dog wants it to end.&quot; The dog will then end the spell whenever it wishes. The dog will have no power to turn it back on again, spells don't come with on/off switches, they're either going or they're not. The closest you can come to turning them on and off is to use spells or WP boosted Withstand to temporarily suppress them.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is personal preference and not a strict reading of RAW, but I would not allow that condition. Something like the target &quot;wanting&quot; the spell to end is way too nebulous and hard to arbitrate, so I would insist on the trigger being some unambiguous action, like saying a certain word or, in the case of a dog, licking their left paw three times or something. Either way you would have to somehow get the dog to understand how to disable the effect, which would involve either intense training or further magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T09:02:02-07:00","id":1131735,"title":"","content":"Thanks to everyone for their input.<br /> It looks like, under RAW, I can't really do everything I want to do (which includes effectively giving the familiar abilities which can be activated / discontinued on permanent level). I don't want the creature just to be a convenient target for spells - I want to give it full time upgrades.<br /> I may be limited to making him faster / stronger / smarter. I guess luckier is also an option. And maybe if my character picks up some Prime there is some way to let him store Mana too ...<br /> <br /> I was planning on making a character that primary concentrated on Death, Life, and Mind, but would get a bit of Fate and Prime as well in time.<br /> <br /> One of my first buffs was going to give the (probably) dog the ability to bite/interact with ghosts with the touch of the grave effect, but having that on full time seems like it would be more vulnerability than strength. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T09:13:50-07:00","id":1131740,"title":"","content":"If it is a central part of your character and you want these effects that are only doable with great difficulty you could consider dedicating a legacy to it and instead of gaining attainments for yourself the familiar gains abilities as you progress and the bond grows closer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T09:19:17-07:00","id":1131742,"title":"","content":"You know what you could do? An Imbued Item. It's probably the most efficient way of giving a non-Mage the ability to cast a given spell. It takes quite a bit of Prime, but I'm sure you can ferret out some contact in the Consilium to justify taking the Merit at least.<br /> <br /> But also, doing stupid wizard things is kind of a theme in Mage. Getting your dog mauled by ghosts because you thought it would be cool to have a permanent pet Barghest is precisely the sort of hubristic &quot;oh shit&quot; mistake an inexperienced Death/Life specialist would make.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T09:52:52-07:00","id":1131756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131419-alternative-familiar-ideas?p=1131740#post1131740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it is a central part of your character and you want these effects that are only doable with great difficulty you could consider dedicating a legacy to it and instead of gaining attainments for yourself the familiar gains abilities as you progress and the bond grows closer.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is an interesting idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T11:01:30-07:00","id":1131785,"title":"","content":"If you go that route further considerations may include:<br /> Do you turn your familar into a soul stone?<br /> What happens should the familiar you've forged your soul to die?<br /> (What if you die and the familiar lives? Do you get to warg ala GoT?)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T11:40:58-07:00","id":1131807,"title":"","content":"Turning your familiar into a soul stone would automatically grant it the Connected Sympathy status that familiars typically enjoy. So that's an option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T11:52:32-07:00","id":1131815,"title":"","content":"It also would allow you to share its senses after a fashion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T12:10:23-07:00","id":1131823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131419-alternative-familiar-ideas?p=1131815#post1131815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also would allow you to share its senses after a fashion.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would make having your &quot;familiar&quot; captured even more dangerous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T12:18:12-07:00","id":1131831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131419-alternative-familiar-ideas?p=1131823#post1131823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It would make having your &quot;familiar&quot; captured even more dangerous.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not particularly more dangerous than having a regular familiar captured. Afaik the main danger of a soul stone falling into the wrong hands is that it has a Connected sympathetic tie with you, and so does a familiar. I guess you could have have the Familiar spell destroyed if the entity is captured, but I suspect an entity that was your familiar until three seconds ago will probably still have at least a Strong connection.<br /> <br /> e: and it probably won't appreciate you ditching it at the first sign of trouble","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T12:33:47-07:00","id":1131837,"title":"","content":"I think soul stones have to be inanimate. The rules for them always call them an &quot;object&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T12:48:58-07:00","id":1131842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131419-alternative-familiar-ideas?p=1131837#post1131837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think soul stones have to be inanimate. The rules for them always call them an &quot;object&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume a Prime/Life spell could fix that problem. I'd probably require it in fact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T14:59:02-07:00","id":1131898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131419-alternative-familiar-ideas?p=1131831#post1131831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not particularly more dangerous than having a regular familiar captured. Afaik the main danger of a soul stone falling into the wrong hands is that it has a Connected sympathetic tie with you, and so does a familiar. I guess you could have have the Familiar spell destroyed if the entity is captured, but I suspect an entity that was your familiar until three seconds ago will probably still have at least a Strong connection.<br /> <br /> e: and it probably won't appreciate you ditching it at the first sign of trouble</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking more along the lines that per RAW, it is perfectly acceptable for a mage who has a soul stone to demand services (up to three) before returning it. This gives them a lever over you that doesn't require them to directly attack you through the familiar (which act I imagine may give you a valid chance to get redress from the local concilium).. Unless that &quot;three services&quot; rule about soul stones was ditched in 2ed and I missed it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T15:00:22-07:00","id":1131899,"title":"","content":"No, it's still there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T15:58:53-07:00","id":1131928,"title":"","content":"Just because it is the established method for resolving conflict when something as sensitive as a soul stone has been acquired by another mage, doesn't mean it is acceptable under the lex magica to just go ahead and steal another mages soul stone. You'd probably violate their sanctum at least in most cases. In the end it heavily depends on the local consilium how such a thing would be handled (as the lex is heavily open to interpretation).<br /> <br /> All of this said a mage could conceivably also try to extort favour(s) by holding a familar hostage.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T10:19:03-07:00","id":1133065,"title":"","content":"It wouldn't be a very good strategy, the Mage could simply sever the familiar arrangement and the kidnapper loses his leverage. Though I suppose it would work on the sentimental types.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T10:34:55-07:00","id":1133073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131419-alternative-familiar-ideas?p=1133065#post1133065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It wouldn't be a very good strategy, the Mage could simply sever the familiar arrangement and the kidnapper loses his leverage. Though I suppose it would work on the sentimental types.</div> </div> </div> </div>I sincerely doubt the sympathetic connection between a mage and her familiar would drop to nothing the instant you sever the bond. That's probably still a Strong connection.<br /> <br /> Plus you have the inherent leverage that even the most cold-hearted mage probably wants her familiar back regardless of whether the captor intends to abuse its sympathetic link to her or not. Getting a new one is going to be a pain, especially if the relevant community of mages and/or ephemeral entities learns that you left your last familiar to die as soon as it became a liability to you.<br /> <br /> e: hell it's almost certainly a violation of whatever bargain you struck to gain a familiar in the first place, leaving you open to censure under the Lex Magica and quite possibly also the laws of the spirit courts/Underworld/etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13628,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","user":"Terrorforge","date":". 08-23-2017, 01:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T15:20:57-07:00","id":1133185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131419-alternative-familiar-ideas?p=1133073#post1133073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I sincerely doubt the sympathetic connection between a mage and her familiar would drop to nothing the instant you sever the bond. That's probably still a Strong connection.<br /> <br /> Plus you have the inherent leverage that even the most cold-hearted mage probably wants her familiar back regardless of whether the captor intends to abuse its sympathetic link to her or not. Getting a new one is going to be a pain, especially if the relevant community of mages and/or ephemeral entities learns that you left your last familiar to die as soon as it became a liability to you.<br /> <br /> e: hell it's almost certainly a violation of whatever bargain you struck to gain a familiar in the first place, leaving you open to censure under the Lex Magica and quite possibly also the laws of the spirit courts/Underworld/etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a bit of a tangent, but part of the reason I started the thread is because I liked the concept of familiar as best friend present in Ars Magica. I never thought the current edition of MtAw portrayed familiars as anything but useful allies and (sort of) business partners. Spirits etc. are alien enough (a dog spirit is NOT a dog) that I never got the impression there was much fellow feeling between a familiar and his mage or vice versa. Your response (among others) seems to assume this as well. I'm curious if anyone plays familiars as they are in the game now as though they had any real sentimental attachment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T15:39:13-07:00","id":1133191,"title":"","content":"Well, with Spirit 5 you can create a bespoke spirit that could theoretically think more like a human does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T15:42:12-07:00","id":1133194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131419-alternative-familiar-ideas?p=1133185#post1133185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is a bit of a tangent, but part of the reason I started the thread is because I liked the concept of familiar as best friend present in Ars Magica. I never thought the current edition of MtAw portrayed familiars as anything but useful allies and (sort of) business partners. Spirits etc. are alien enough (a dog spirit is NOT a dog) that I never got the impression there was much fellow feeling between a familiar and his mage or vice versa. Your response (among others) seems to assume this as well. I'm curious if anyone plays familiars as they are in the game now as though they had any real sentimental attachment.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was mostly responding to Mrmdubois' comment and trying to show that even if you aren't &quot;the sentimental type&quot; the solution isn't great. I actually think the #1 reason most mages wouldn't do that is that they aren't monsters. When I say it would displease the local mages I don't just mean it in the dry, robotic sense of &quot;you have violated your oath and endangered our relationship with the local spirit courts and will therefore face punishment according to-&quot;. I very much mean it in the sense of &quot;nobody, especially not spirit/death/mind/whatever mages, will want anything to do with you because what you did was pretty fucked up.&quot; Abandoning what is ostensibly your closest ally to an enemy because you're scared they'll use your sympathetic link against is the kind of thing that leaves a big, permanent stain on your reputation, and for good reason.<br /> <br /> It obviously depends on what relationship the player wants with their familiar, but I would absolutely play it as a friendship - albeit with a peculiar entity that doesn't quite have the same understanding of what &quot;friendship&quot; means as a human. Spirits may be weird and alien, but they definitely have subjective opinions and do form relationships and pack bonds, especially if it's a spirit of something like a dog that's already a pack animal. And honestly, even if the entity in question was completely incapable of experiencing anything a human would recognize as &quot;friendship&quot;, humans have a massive tendency to get attached to and anthropomorphize objects and animals, so I think it's very likely that even if the entity is only in it for coldly logical reasons, the mage will probably grow attached to her ethereal pal anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T15:48:47-07:00","id":1133197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131419-alternative-familiar-ideas?p=1133191#post1133191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> spirit that could theoretically think more like a human does.</div> </div> </div> </div>What could go wrong...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T15:49:12-07:00","id":1133198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131419-alternative-familiar-ideas?p=1133185#post1133185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious if anyone plays familiars as they are in the game now as though they had any real sentimental attachment.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a mage whose familiar is her own ghost (through some convoluted fuckery that took place during her Awakening). They functioned, at the worst of times, like resentful siblings that still clearly loved each other, and at the best of times like twins that spent their existence consistently operating on the same wavelength.<br /> <br /> Neither of them would have ever done anything to put the other in jeopardy - they were the only 'family' either one had left, and they grew highly emotionally interdependent throughout the course of the Chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T17:48:11-07:00","id":1133230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131419-alternative-familiar-ideas?p=1133194#post1133194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I actually think the #1 reason most mages wouldn't do that is that they aren't monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Mages <i>are</i> monsters&quot; is one of the core conceits of the game, though...<br /> <br /> That said, a Sympathetic connection that strong may start as purely transactional, but that level of metaphysical closeness will inevitably create something more<i>. </i>Think something like a stage-three blood bond, the Mage wouldn't <i>want</i> to abandon their familiar any more than they'd want to abandon a Soul stone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}